Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:30:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 32/40] PROTOTYPE pvr: one clip rectangle per transfer pass

With two clip rectangles in one transfer prepare the TQ emits to two PBE
render targets. On a GX6250 the second was never written and the first
had holes, and RGBA8 copies page-faulted the fragment data master: a
vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer of a 203x117 RGBA8 image into a tight buffer did,
every time. The case is a double-stride copy (odd row length) with an odd
height, whose even- and odd-row halves differ in height and cannot merge
into one rectangle.

Allow one clip rectangle per pass, so each becomes its own prepare (and
job, with the previous patch). Root cause in the multi-target emission
not found; this is a workaround.

Generated-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 65a39f97295136f98ec9c4abde5957c3c6c2cfc4)
(cherry picked from commit 606f3896df7d41b2cafbb36fb653008a5efce5b1)
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_transfer.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_transfer.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_transfer.c
index 4648ffa6a58..9a3df8a6810 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_transfer.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_transfer.c
@@ -5693,7 +5693,13 @@ static VkResult pvr_3d_copy_blit(struct pvr_transfer_ctx *ctx,
    }
 
    if (pass_idx == 0U) {
-      pvr_get_custom_mapping(dev_info, active_cmd, 3U, &state->custom_mapping);
+      /* PROTOTYPE: one clip rectangle (one PBE render target) per pass. On
+       * a GX6250 a transfer prepare with two render targets wrote nothing for
+       * the second and left holes in the first, and page-faulted for RGBA8
+       * (e.g. the even/odd-row halves of a double-stride copy with an odd
+       * height). Separate passes are separate jobs.
+       */
+      pvr_get_custom_mapping(dev_info, active_cmd, 1U, &state->custom_mapping);
 
       if (state->custom_mapping.texel_extend_src > 1U)
          state->custom_mapping.texel_extend_dst = 1U;
